Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the **Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area**. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Under the council's windows guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material or the design (for example, switching from timber to uPVC, or altering the glazing pattern), you will likely need to apply. If you are replacing like for like, you may not need to, but I'd recommend confirming that with the planning team before you start, since I can't give a formal planning opinion.
